# SpecWithCode release settings for scripts/release/release.sh: paths and ids only, never a secret.
# Copy to ~/.config/skill-studio-release/release.env (outside every repository) and chmod 600.
# release.sh sources it, checks that each file exists and each value is set, and prints no values.

# Developer ID Application certificate (.p12) and the file holding its passphrase (mode 600).
CSC_LINK_PATH="$HOME/.config/skill-studio-release/cert/developerID_application.p12"
CSC_PASSPHRASE_FILE="$HOME/.config/skill-studio-release/cert/p12.passphrase"

# App Store Connect API key for notarization: the .p8 file, its key id and the issuer id.
APPLE_API_KEY_PATH="$HOME/.config/skill-studio-release/AuthKey_KEYID.p8"
APPLE_API_KEY_ID="KEYID"
APPLE_API_ISSUER="00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"

# The built-in Google OAuth pair: a mode-600 file with only STUDIO_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID and
# STUDIO_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET. Set GOOGLE_OAUTH_SOURCE_ENV once to have preflight copy those
# two lines out of another env file; it never copies anything else.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENV_FILE="$HOME/.config/skill-studio-release/google-oauth.env"
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_SOURCE_ENV="$HOME/path/to/an/.env"

# SpecWithCode Connect public values (identifiers, not secrets). With all four set, the build
# ships Connect on; leave them unset to build without it. See docs/operations/connect-launch.md.
# STUDIO_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="pk_live_..."
# STUDIO_CLERK_JWT_TEMPLATE="studio-relay"
# STUDIO_CLERK_CLI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID="..."
# STUDIO_RELAY_URL="https://relay.spec-weave.com"

# Toolchain. release.sh drops anaconda from PATH and puts nvm's Node first.
NODE_VERSION="22.20.0"
SDKROOT="/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/Developer/SDKs/MacOSX26.2.sdk"

# Optional overrides (defaults shown).
# PUBLIC_CLONE="$HOME/Projects/github/release.noindex/public"
# STUDIO_PUBLIC_RULES="$HOME/.local/share/specweave/specwithcode-public/rules.json"
# STUDIO_FLEET_HOSTS="$HOME/.local/share/specweave/fleet/hosts.json"
# The public clone's own commit identity; the email must be a GitHub noreply address.
# PUBLIC_GIT_NAME="Anton Abyzov"
# PUBLIC_GIT_EMAIL="979819+anton-abyzov@users.noreply.github.com"
